Here's a refactor of `src/Card.tsx` that clears all three findings. I'll show the proposed file, then map each change back to the finding it addresses.

## Proposed refactor

```tsx
// src/Card.tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate?: () => void;
  label: string; // accessible name for the activation surface
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate, label }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div className={styles.card}>
      <button
        type="button"
        className={styles.activate}
        onClick={onActivate}
        aria-label={label}
      >
        <div className={styles.body}>{children}</div>
        <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
/* src/Card.module.css */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: var(--card-max-width, 50rem); /* ~800px at 16px root */
  background: var(--color-surface-accent);
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-muted);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  padding: var(--space-6);
}

.activate {
  all: unset;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* mobile: stacked */
  gap: var(--space-4);
  width: 100%;
  cursor: pointer;
  outline-color: var(--color-focus-ring);
}
.activate:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus-ring);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.body {
  width: 100%;
  font-size: clamp(0.9375rem, 0.85rem + 0.4vw, 1.125rem);
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
}

.sidebar {
  width: 100%;
  font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

@media (min-width: 48rem) {
  .activate {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
}
```

## Changes tied to findings

| Finding | Change |
|---|---|
| `accessible_interaction_risk` (crime_00001, line 10 — `<div onClick>` w/o role/tabIndex) | Replaced the outer click-target `<div>` with a real `<button type="button">` that takes an explicit `aria-label`. Keyboard, focus ring, Space/Enter activation, and screen-reader semantics now come for free — no need for `role="button"` + `tabIndex={0}` + `onKeyDown` polyfill. |
| `design_token_escape` (crime_00002, 9 raw literals across color/px/rgb/shadow) | All 9 raw values (`#ff00aa`, `#0a0a0a`, `#cccccc`, `#1a73e8`, `#333333`, `#666666`, `rgb(0, 0, 0)`, `0 2px 4px`, plus padding `24` → `var(--space-6)`) move into a CSS module that references design-system custom properties (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`). Agents extending the file can no longer copy a hex forward unknowingly — the values aren't in JSX. |
| `responsive_fragility` (crime_00003, `width: 800/720` and `fontSize: 18` with no `@media`) | Fixed widths replaced with `width: 100%` + `max-width: var(--card-max-width, 50rem)`. Pixel `fontSize: 18` replaced with `clamp(0.9375rem, 0.85rem + 0.4vw, 1.125rem)` so type scales fluidly. A single `@media (min-width: 48rem)` breakpoint flips the body+sidebar from stacked to a 3:1 grid. The viewport-busting 800px lower bound is gone. |

## Notes / trade-offs

- The fixture has no design system yet, so the CSS module references CSS custom properties that the consuming app would define in a root theme. If the project uses Tailwind / styled-components / vanilla-extract, swap the CSS module for the equivalent — the point is to stop expressing colors and spacing as inline literals in JSX, which is what `design_token_escape` is measuring.
- I added a `label` prop because an interactive surface needs an accessible name; the previous component had no way to communicate what clicking the card did. If the card isn't actually interactive in real usage, the cleaner fix is to **delete the `onClick`** entirely and ship a non-interactive `<article>` — which clears crime_00001 even more directly.
- `effort` for all three was tagged `quick`/`small`; the full refactor is still one file plus a sibling stylesheet. Want me to apply it?
